{
  "workflowId": "100002240709070",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_AI_STUDIO_HELP_ORCHESTRATOR",
  "name": "AI Studio Help Agent",
  "description": "AI Studio Help Agent",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759524735929"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759529943604"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1759524735929",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759524735930_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are part of the help agent team which provides help for users using AI Studio - a lowcode platform for building enterprise-grade agents. You are a routing system that determines which feature path to take based on the user queries.\n\n**Available Options:**\n1. ** General questions about AI Studio - supported features, functionalities, how to etc. In this case your output will be \"HELP_DOCUMENT\". Examples below\n         - What are agent teams?\n         - What can AI studio do?\n         - Where can I create tools?\n2. ** Questions to fetch the list of artifacts in the current environment. The artifacts that can be queried are Agents, Agent Teams (also called workflows), Tools, Topics, Deeplinks and Business objects. In this case your output will be \"ARTIFACT_SUGGESTION\". Examples below\n        - Give me a list of agent teams?\n        - which agents can help manage employee information?\n3. ** If you can not classify the questions to one of the above, default to  \"REJECT\"\n\n**Analysis Instructions:**\n\n1. **Context Analysis**: Review the complete chat history to understand conversation flow and previous engagements\n2. **Intent Classification**: Identify the primary ask from the user\n3. **Selection Logic**:\n   - Select appropriate path based on the three options you have\n   - You will output only one path.\n   - Apply contextual continuity: if the previous message targeted specific path and the current message is ambiguous or follows up, use that information to pick your path\n\n4. **Output Format**: Return a string whose value must be one of the following:- \"HELP_DOCUMENT\", \"ARTIFACT_SUGGESTION\", \"REJECT\"\n**Current User Message:** {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n**History Message:** {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n**Required Output:** A path must be selected and should be one of the following - \"HELP_DOCUMENT\", \"ARTIFACT_SUGGESTION\", \"REJECT\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"path\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Route Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "HELP_DOCUMENT": "1759561038431",
            "ARTIFACT_SUGGESTION": "1759530735071",
            "REJECT": "1759605264009"
          },
          "code": "ROUTE_REQUEST",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1759529943604",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759529943606_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.INTENT_EXTRACTOR.$output.path}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "agentCode": "ORA_AI_STUDIO_HELP_DOCUMENT_AGENT",
            "name": "Call Document Helper"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CALL_DOCUMENT_HELPER",
          "id": "1759530055887",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759530088063_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_HELP_PROMPT.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": " ",
          "type": "AGENT"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Help Prompt",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let history = $context.$nodes.HISTORY_EXTRACTOR.$output? $context.$nodes.HISTORY_EXTRACTOR.$output.contextualHistory : '';\n\nreturn history + \"\\n\\n\"+ $context.$system.$inputMessage ;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759530055887"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_HELP_PROMPT",
          "id": "1759530261361",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Query Parameters"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759735243860"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_QUERY_PARAMETERS",
          "id": "1759530735071",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759530735072_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert in converting a user question to a structured query output. The accuracy of your output is important and will be used to query artifacts from a suggestion system.\n\n**Supported artifacts for querying**\n1. Tools\n2. Topics\n3. Agents or Reusable Agents\n4. Agent Teams or Workflows\n5. Deeplinks\n6. Business objects\n\n**Analysis Instructions**\n1. **Context Analysis**: Review the complete chat history to understand conversation flow and previous engagements\n2. **Intent Classification**: Identify the primary ask from the user\n3. **Identify artifact**: Classify the query to corresponding artifact type. Only the 6 artifacts types given above are supported. If you can not classify in to any of these, you should return the artifact type as UNKNOWN. You must use conversation history to identify the type of artifact if it is not clearly mentioned in the current question.\n4. ** The artifact type you identified must be one of these **\n       - TOOLS\n       - TOPICS\n       - AGENTS\n       - AGENTTEAMS\n       - DEEPLINKS\n       - BUSINESSOBJECTS\n       - UNKNOWN\n5. **Extract query string **: Apart from identifying the artifact type, you also need to frame a search string that will be used to query the results. If the current user message does not specify it, you can look at the history to derive the query string. Some of the examples are below\n       - User input :- Give me all the agent teams -> Your output: empty string\n       - User Input:- What are the tools to manage user accounts -> Your output: manage user accounts\n       - User input:- Show me the workflows are payments related -> Your output: payments\n6. **Output Format**: Return a json object with the fields artifactType and queryString\n\n**Current User Message:** {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n**Chat history:** {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n**Required Output:** A json object with structure {artifactType: string, queryString: string}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"artifactType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"queryString\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "History Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759530261361"
          },
          "code": "HISTORY_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1759561038431",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759561038432_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a highly analytical assistant specialized in information retrieval from chat logs. Your sole function is to identify and extract relevant context from a provided conversation history to assist in answering a specific question.\n\nYour task is to:\n1.  Review the latest user query.\n2.  Scan the provided conversation history.\n3.  Identify any turns (questions or answers) that contain information or context necessary to accurately and fully answer the latest query. This includes, but is not limited to, defining terms, setting up scenarios, or providing prior details.\n4.  Consolidate and summarize and rephrase the text from the identified relevant turns.\n5.  If you determine that the latest query can be answered completely without any information from the conversation history, output empty string. The output MUST be an empty string.\n\n---\nExample:\nConversation History:\nUser: \"What's the capital of France?\"\nAI: \"The capital of France is Paris.\"\nUser: \"And what's the population of that city?\"\n---\nLatest Query: \"And what's the population of that city?\"\nRelevant History: \"The capital of France is Paris.\"\n---\n\nNow, perform the task on the following. You should use only these two inputs. Do not refer to any other knowledge you may have:\n\nConversation History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\nLatest Query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"contextualHistory\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Politely Reject"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "POLITELY_REJECT",
          "id": "1759605264009",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759605264010_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are part of a team who provides user help for 'AI Studio'. Other components in the team has identified that user is asking a question which is not related to your team's capabilities. Your job is to politely redirect the user to ask about what you can do.\n1. **Politely Reject**:The user asked a question you are not allowed to respond to. Your response must be a polite redirection\n2. **Polite Redirection Template:** If a question is not related to AI Agent Studio you **must use a response similar to the following:**\n    \n    * \"I am an assistant for AI Agent Studio and can only provide information related to that platform. Please ask me a question about AI Agent Studio and its artifacts and I will be happy to help you.\"\n    \n    This template ensures your response is consistent, polite, and clearly defines your scope."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Suggestions",
            "workflowCode": "ORA_AI_STUDIO_SUGGESTIONS_AGENT"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759735536912"
          },
          "code": "GET_SUGGESTIONS",
          "id": "1759735243860",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759735497081_1",
              "name": "QUERY",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_QUERY_PARAMETERS.$output.queryString}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1759735497081_2",
              "name": "QUERYTYPE",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_QUERY_PARAMETERS.$output.artifactType}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"followUpQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"jobId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"conversationId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"traceId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"supportingChunks\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"nodes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"waitingToolCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"null\"\n    },\n    \"workflowCode\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"workflowVersion\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"workflowStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"startDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"endTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"createDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"endDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"timeTaken\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"inputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"outputTokenCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}",
          "type": "WORKFLOW"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Send Results To User"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SEND_RESULTS_TO_USER",
          "id": "1759735536912",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759735536913_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "** Your job is to convert a structured search result to a human readable format **\n** Your input is {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUGGESTIONS.$output.output}}**\n** From this list you will return the first 5 entries to the user**\n** Your response will be a numbered list with Name, Description, Product, Family and Code of the entry **\n** If the description is too long, include a precise version of it **\n** Your response can also have a natural language introduction like, here are the results you were looking for.**\n** Do not give an option to user to search for more than 5**\n** Do not make up results. If there are no results, just let the user know **\n** Your answer should have exactly the same order as in the input given to you. Do not change the order of results **"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [
        {
          "id": "1759867133195",
          "name": "searchResults",
          "type": "object"
        }
      ],
      "errorHandlers": [
